# List navigation aliases

Down and Up, and their aliases `C-j` and `C-k`, move by one row.
`M-down` and `M-up` jump to the last and first selectable rows.

Create four plain sessions so single-row movement and jumps to either end have
different destinations in the unfiltered picker.

    :b jj cat (available)
    :cp tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :t new-session -d -s alpha "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s beta "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s gamma "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s zeta "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s ui "smth" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 100 -y 12 (success)
    :p ui:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)

Hide the preview so the selected row movement is easy to inspect.

    :k C-p
    :snap

```terminal
session:                                                                                           ┃
  6/6 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                                          ┃
▌■ runner                                                                                          ┃
 ■ alpha                                                                                           ┃
 ■ beta                                                                                            ┃
 ■ gamma                                                                                           ┃
 ■ zeta                                                                                            ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] flag, [C-t] tags                                                               ┃
```

Down moves the selection down by one row.

    :k down
    :snap

```terminal
session:                                                                                           ┃
  6/6 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                                          ┃
 ■ runner                                                                                          ┃
▌■ alpha                                                                                           ┃
 ■ beta                                                                                            ┃
 ■ gamma                                                                                           ┃
 ■ zeta                                                                                            ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] flag, [C-t] tags                                                               ┃
```

Up moves the selection back up by one row.

    :k up
    :snap

```terminal
